{"abstract":"Orthomyxo- and bunyaviruses steal the 5′ cap portion of host RNAs to prime their own transcription in a process called “cap snatching.” We report that RNA modification of the cap portion by host 2′-O-ribose methyltransferase 1 (MTr1) is essential for the initiation of influenza A and B virus replication, but not for other cap-snatching viruses. We identified with in silico compound screening and functional analysis a derivative of a natural product from Streptomyces, called trifluoromethyl-tubercidin (TFMT), that inhibits MTr1 through interaction at its S-adenosyl-L-methionine binding pocket to restrict influenza virus replication. Mechanistically, TFMT impairs the association of host cap RNAs with the viral polymerase basic protein 2 subunit in human lung explants and in vivo in mice. TFMT acts synergistically with approved anti-influenza drugs.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Tsukamoto, Yuta","Hiono, Takahiro","Yamada, Shintaro","Matsuno, Keita","Faist, Aileen","Claff, Tobias","Hou, Jianyu","Namasivayam, Vigneshwaran","vom Hemdt, Anja","Sugimoto, Satoko","Ng, Jin Ying","Christensen, Maria H.","Tesfamariam, Yonas M.","Wolter, Steven","Juranek, Stefan","Zillinger, Thomas","Bauer, Stefan","Hirokawa, Takatsugu","Schmidt, Florian I.","Kochs, Georg","Shimojima, Masayuki","Huang, Yi Shuian","Pichlmair, Andreas","Kümmerer, Beate M.","Sakoda, Yoshihiro","Schlee, Martin","Brunotte, Linda","Müller, Christa E.","Igarashi, Manabu","Kato, Hiroki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-260367"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Igarashi, Manabu","Kato, Hiroki"],"country":["Germany","Japan","Taiwan"],"glorg":["Academia Sinica Taiwan","All Global Affiliations","Hokkaido University","National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology","National Institute of Infectious Diseases","Technical University of Munich","University of Bonn","University of Freiburg","University of Marburg","University of Münster","University of Tsukuba"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inhibition of cellular rna methyltransferase abrogates influenza virus capping and replication","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85147791545","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-260367","identifier":[{"id":"36758070","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85147791545","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e57afff0-1209-4d3e-92f4-f592420aad55"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67F9AFD8DD13A78A6E165547F3E2E894"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bonn","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"jp","key":"hokkaido university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Hokkaido University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of münster","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Münster","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"jp","key":"national institute of infectious diseases","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"National Institute of Infectious Diseases","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus U