,"corresponding":null,"first":"Masayuki","key":"shimojimapau","last":"Shimojima","name":"Shimojima, Masayuki","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi Shuian","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Yi Shuian","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 12","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","name":"Pichlmair, Andreas","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Beate M.","key":"kümmererpau","last":"Kümmerer","name":"Kümmerer, Beate M.","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yoshihiro","key":"sakodapau","last":"Sakoda","name":"Sakoda, Yoshihiro","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"schleepau","last":"Schlee","name":"Schlee, Martin","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Linda","key":"brunottepau","last":"Brunotte","name":"Brunotte, Linda","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christa E.","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Christa E.","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Manabu","key":"igarashipau","last":"Igarashi","name":"Igarashi, Manabu","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hiroki","key":"katopau","last":"Kato","name":"Kato, Hiroki","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36758070"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1126/science.add0875","issn":["00368075","10959203"],"issn_org":["00368075"],"issue":"6632","journal":"Science","pages":"586-591","publisher":"American Association for the Advancement of Science","status":"p","title":"Science","volume":"379"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147791545"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e57afff0-1209-4d3e-92f4-f592420aad55"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Inhibition of cellular RNA methyltransferase abrogates influenza virus capping and replication","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-260367","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Game feel design is the intentional design of the affective impact of moment-to-moment interaction with games. In this article, we survey academic research and publications by practitioners to give a complete overview of the state of research concerning this aspect of game design. We analyzed over 200 sources and categorized their content according to design purposes. This resulted in three different domains of intended player experiences: 1) physicality; 2) amplification; and 3) support. In these domains, the act of polishing, which determines game feel, takes the shape of tuning, juicing, and streamlining, respectively. Tuning the physicality of game objects creates cohesion and predictability, and the resulting movement informs level design. Juicing is the act of polishing amplification and it results in empowerment and provides clarity of feedback. Streamlining allows a game to act on the intention of the player, supporting the execution of actions in the game. These three design intents are the main means through which designers control minute details of interactivity and inform the player’s reaction. The presented framework and its nuanced vocabulary can lead to an understanding of game feel that is shared between practitioners and researchers as highlighted in the concluding future research section.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pichlmair, Martin","Johansen, Mads"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384924"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Game design","Video games","game feel","game feel design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing game feel a survey","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/91131028/TG3072241.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384924","identifier":[{"id":"85104170588","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f85b6568-f9e9-41ff-bb40-aabd2f27b736"],"keyword":["game design","game feel","game feel design","video games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E0C642BDE37950978650729F1CEA139"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/91131028/TG3072241.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","locid":"ddcdfda8-c5ea-4e67-b0ea-21ba86966197","name":"Pichlmair, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8828-9723","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Mads","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tg.2021.3072241","issn":["24751502","24751510"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Games","pages":"138","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Games","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104170588"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f85b6568-f9e9-41ff-bb40-aabd2f27b736"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing Game Feel: A Survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384924","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a Mixed-Initiative version of Squeezer, a tool for designing juice effects in the Unity game engine. Drawing upon sound synthesizers and game description languages, Squeezer can synthesize common types of juice effects by combining simple building blocks into sequences. Additionally, Squeezer offers effect generation based on predefined recipes as well as an interface for interactively evolving effect sequences. We conducted a user study with five experts to verify the functionality and interest among game designers. By applying generative and evolutionary strategies to juice effect design, Squeezer allows game designers and researchers using games in their work to explore adding juice effects to their games and frameworks. Squeezer is available at: https://github.com/pyjamads/Squeezer","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Mads","Pichlmair, Martin","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383423"],"event":{"acronym":"FGD(?)","end":"2021-08-06","place":"Fully Online","start":"2021-08-02","title":"FDG 2021: Foundations of Digital Games","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Generative design strategies","Juice Effects","Mixed initiative tools","Sound synthesis","Unity game engine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"squeezer a mixed initiative tool for designing juice effects","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3472538.3472575","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383423","identifier":[{"id":"85118238023","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-92eafb4f-70ba-42f8-a317-90746d2b4d4f"],"keyword":["Generative design strategies","Juice effects","Mixed-initiative tools","Sound synthesis","Unity game engine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7844109C88C62C31017234C9A0B1FA25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3472538.3472575","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86237995/Squeezer_Evolution_FDG_pure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Mads","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","locid":"ddcdfda8-c5ea-4e67-b0ea-21ba86966197","name":"Pichlmair, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8828-9723","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3472538.3472575","eisbn":["9781450384223/21/08"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of The 16th International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games (FDG) 2021 (FDG’21)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118238023"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-92eafb4f-70ba-42f8-a317-90746d2b4d4f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Squeezer - A Mixed-Initiative Tool for Designing Juice Effects","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383423","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a series of experiments that map the expressive space of specific procedural generation techniques with playful aleatory interventions. They are tools for inspiration based on divinatory practices. This paper connects these ancient procedural techniques to contemporary technologies like Twitter bots. We challenge the limits of these technologies in order to playfully explore the role they can play in everyday life. The first experiment, Nostrandomus, remixes ancient prophecies. The second one, Five Sparrows on a Vampire, generates proposals for dining experiences featuring recipes and accompanying eating instructions. The third tool, Haikookies, is a self-help inspired twitter bot that shares fortune cookie-style wisdom in haiku form. The final experiment, Tiphareth, is a set of partially procedurally generated tarot cards. Additionally, Ephemerald, a tool for streamlined Tracery-based [6] procedural content generation is introduced. The takeaway of this paper is that data curation is a fundamental component of working with generative systems. In other words, the human aspect needs to be present in order to create meaningful results.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pichlmair, Martin","Putney, Charlene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382946"],"event":{"acronym":"FGD(?)","title":"Foundations of Digital Games"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Contemporary Technologies","Data Curation","Divinatory Practices","Playful Aleatory Interventions","Procedural Generation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"procedural generation for divination and inspiration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85520310/Divination_7.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382946","identifier":[{"id":"85092312297","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7102ac9f-7cbf-42a6-8d3d-e17da40d994d"],"keyword":["Contemporary Technologies","Data Curation","Divinatory Practices","Playful Aleatory Interventions","Procedural Generation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D45665A654836B3F5666A1D1BBF664EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85520310/Divination_7.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","locid":"ddcdfda8-c5ea-4e67-b0ea-21ba86966197","name":"Pichlmair, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8828-9723","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlene","key":"putneypau","last":"Putney","name":"Putney, Charlene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3402942.3402950","eisbn":["9781450388078"],"place":"Bugibba Malta","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"FDG '20: International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092312297"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7102ac9f-7cbf-42a6-8d3d-e17da40d994d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Procedural Generation for Divination and Inspiration","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382946","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces Squeezer, a tool for designing juicy effects inthe Unity game engine. Drawing upon inspiration from sound effect synthesizers and description languages, Squeezer can \"synthesize\" common types of juice effects, by combining simple effects into effect sequences. These effect sequences can be edited and executed even while playing the game in the editor, lowering iteration times and easing the exploration of effects. We make a preliminary usability test to verify the functionality and scope of the tool. Squeezer is available at: https://github.com/pyjamads/Squeezer","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Mads","Pichlmair, Martin","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384263"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Game Development","Game design","Generators","Interaction Feedback","Juice Effects","Prototyping","Toolkit"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"squeezer a tool for designing juicy effects","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85551062/Squeezer_WiP_camera_ready_nonacm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384263","identifier":[{"id":"85096789311","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ccbd50e4-4265-4f31-b3f8-426241b47d99"],"keyword":["Game Design","Game Development","Generators","Interaction Feedback","Juice Effects","Prototyping","Toolkit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-14E1534DE623865C178C22FB6928D976"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85551062/Squeezer_WiP_camera_ready_nonacm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Mads","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","locid":"ddcdfda8-c5ea-4e67-b0ea-21ba86966197","name":"Pichlmair, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8828-9723","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3383668.3419862","pages":"282-286","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CHI PLAY '20: Extended Abstracts of the 2020 Annual Symposium on Computer-Human Interaction in Play"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096789311"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ccbd50e4-4265-4f31-b3f8-426241b47d99"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Squeezer - A Tool for Designing Juicy Effects","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384263","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces UnityVGDL, a port of the Video Game Description Language (VGDL) to the widely used Unity game engine. Our framework is based on the General Video Game AI (GVGAI) competition framework and implements its core ontology, including a forward model. It integrates the Unity Machine Learning Agents (ML-Agents) toolkit with VGDL to train and run agents in VGDL-described games. We compare baseline learning results between GVGAI and UnityVGDL across four different games and conclude that the Unity port is comparable to the GVGAI framework. UnityVGDL is available at: https://github.com/pyjamads/UnityVGDL.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Mads","Pichlmair, Martin","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383399"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Forward Model Integration","General Video Game AI GVGAI","Unity Machine Learning Agents ML Agents","UnityVGDL","Video Game Description Language VGDL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"video game description language environment for unity machine learning agents","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84660499/VGDL_in_Unity3D_Pure.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383399","identifier":[{"id":"85073116022","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-911c6c3c-967b-40f0-9669-0bc18ae75b5b"],"keyword":["Forward Model Integration","General Video Game AI (GVGAI)","Unity Machine Learning Agents (ML-Agents)","UnityVGDL","Video Game Description Language (VGDL)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5270711570AFE3CA5277F29F8B422AD7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84660499/VGDL_in_Unity3D_Pure.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Mads","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","locid":"ddcdfda8-c5ea-4e67-b0ea-21ba86966197","name":"Pichlmair, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8828-9723","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cig.2019.8848072","eisbn":["9781728118840"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2019 IEEE Conference on Games (CoG)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073116022"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-911c6c3c-967b-40f0-9669-0bc18ae75b5b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Video Game Description Language Environment for Unity Machine Learning Agents","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383399","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
